# Platinum Angel against "you lose the game" (CR 104.3e): no game effect makes its controller lose (the 2009-10-01 ruling).
# Bot1 casts the Angel on turn 3, then Glorious End on turn 5: the turn ends, and at the beginning of Bot1's next end step,
# turn 7's, its delayed ability says Bot1 loses the game. With the Angel out Bot1 doesn't, and the game goes on into turn 8.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Sol Ring
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Platinum Angel
Glorious End
Mountain
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Platinum Angel.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glorious End.Cast
[T7 Bot1.Main2]
? Delayed = Glorious End
[T8 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Result = InProgress
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Delayed.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Platinum Angel.Tapped = false
